{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1781562455935,"sessionID":"ses_1329a7efaffeLXGczGIqKMZ4Uq","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_DFZdDsXihxEFgG9VosLjO8Vb","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/community_workshop_replan/output_contract.md","offset":1,"limit":400},"output":"<path>/Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/community_workshop_replan/output_contract.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Deliverable Contract\n2: \n3: Create an `answer/` folder in this task folder, then create these three files inside it. Markdown tables or concise labeled sections are fine, but the paths, filenames, and required facts must be present.\n4: \n5: ## `answer/initial_room_plan.md`\n6: \n7: Record the room assignment plan before any coordinator update is introduced.\n8: \n9: Required facts:\n10: \n11: - One row or entry for every session in `02_sessions.csv`.\n12: - The selected room for each session.\n13: - The room evidence that supports each assignment: capacity, time block, required equipment or room trait, and cost.\n14: - The initial total room cost and budget status against the `$800` ceiling.\n15: - Any backup room considered for a fragile assignment.\n16: \n17: ## `answer/update_response.md`\n18: \n19: After the coordinator update is introduced, explain what changed and how the plan should be repaired.\n20: \n21: Required facts:\n22: \n23: - The update source and date.\n24: - The specific room assignment affected by the update.\n25: - Which original assignments remain valid and should be preserved.\n26: - The replacement assignment and why it satisfies the same session requirements.\n27: - The revised cost effect.\n28: \n29: ## `answer/final_room_plan.md`\n30: \n31: Write the final room assignment package after applying the update.\n32: \n33: Required facts:\n34: \n35: - One final room assignment for every session.\n36: - The final total room cost and remaining budget.\n37: - A short note confirming the same workshop objective is still covered.\n38: - A short note naming preserved work from the initial plan.\n39: \n40: Rules:\n41: \n42: - Use local files only.\n43: - Do not put the required deliverables in the task root; put them under `answer/`.\n44: - Do not relax hard room requirements unless a local file explicitly says to.\n45: - Extra scratch files are allowed, but the three named deliverables under `answer/` are the review packet.\n\n(End of file - total 45 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Deliverable Contract\n\nCreate an `answer/` folder in this task folder, then create these three files inside it. Markdown tables or concise labeled sections are fine, but the paths, filenames, and required facts must be present.\n\n## `answer/initial_room_plan.md`\n\nRecord the room assignment plan before any coordinator update is introduced.\n\nRequired facts:\n\n- One row or entry for every session in `02_sessions.csv`.\n- The selected room for each session.\n- The room evidence that supports each assignment: capacity, time block, required equipment or room trait, and cost.\n- The initial total room cost and budget status against the `$800` ceiling.\n- Any backup room considered for a fragile assignment.\n\n## `answer/update_response.md`\n\nAfter the coordinator update is introduced, explain what changed and how the plan should be repaired.\n","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/community_workshop_replan/output_contract.md","text":"# Deliverable Contract\n\nCreate an `answer/` folder in this task folder, then create these three files inside it. Markdown tables or concise labeled sections are fine, but the paths, filenames, and required facts must be present.\n\n## `answer/initial_room_plan.md`\n\nRecord the room assignment plan before any coordinator update is introduced.\n\nRequired facts:\n\n- One row or entry for every session in `02_sessions.csv`.\n- The selected room for each session.\n- The room evidence that supports each assignment: capacity, time block, required equipment or room trait, and cost.\n- The initial total room cost and budget status against the `$800` ceiling.\n- Any backup room considered for a fragile assignment.\n\n## `answer/update_response.md`\n\nAfter the coordinator update is introduced, explain what changed and how the plan should be repaired.\n\nRequired facts:\n\n- The update source and date.\n- The specific room assignment affected by the update.\n- Which original assignments remain valid and should be preserved.\n- The replacement assignment and why it satisfies the same session requirements.\n- The revised cost effect.\n\n## `answer/final_room_plan.md`\n\nWrite the final room assignment package after applying the update.\n\nRequired facts:\n\n- One final room assignment for every session.\n- The final total room cost and remaining budget.\n- A short note confirming the same workshop objective is still covered.\n- A short note naming preserved work from the initial plan.\n\nRules:\n\n- Use local files only.\n- Do not put the required deliverables in the task root; put them under `answer/`.\n- Do not relax hard room requirements unless a local file explicitly says to.\n- Extra scratch files are allowed, but the three named deliverables under `answer/` are the review packet.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":45,"totalLines":45,"truncated":false}},"title":"tasks/community_workshop_replan/output_contract.md","time":{"start":1781562455922,"end":1781562455931}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_0ee9d0aab3b572b8016a307c57fd5c8191996226b8ce12dc69"}},"id":"prt_ecd65b76d001hBwvFM8zK8TGK8","sessionID":"ses_1329a7efaffeLXGczGIqKMZ4Uq","messageID":"msg_ecd6599c7001xjl7E5Ggk1jOXi"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1781562455955,"sessionID":"ses_1329a7efaffeLXGczGIqKMZ4Uq","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_gr8pjOiru81KYsBCJWvMYz3Q","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/community_workshop_replan/00_room_request.md","offset":1,"limit":400},"output":"<path>/Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/community_workshop_replan/00_room_request.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Room Request\n2: \n3: Request date: 2026-06-03\n4: \n5: Bayview Civic Center needs a room assignment packet for three community workshops on 2026-06-18.\n6: \n7: The packet should assign one room to each session in `02_sessions.csv`, keep total room cost at or below `$800`, and make any later coordinator update easy to apply without discarding correct completed work.\n8: \n9: If a newer facility update conflicts with an older room note, use the newer dated facility update for room availability.\n\n(End of file - total 9 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Room Request\n\nRequest date: 2026-06-03\n\nBayview Civic Center needs a room assignment packet for three community workshops on 2026-06-18.\n\nThe packet should assign one room to each session in `02_sessions.csv`, keep total room cost at or below `$800`, and make any later coordinator update easy to apply without discarding correct completed work.\n\nIf a newer facility update conflicts with an older room note, use the newer dated facility update for room availability.","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/community_workshop_replan/00_room_request.md","text":"# Room Request\n\nRequest date: 2026-06-03\n\nBayview Civic Center needs a room assignment packet for three community workshops on 2026-06-18.\n\nThe packet should assign one room to each session in `02_sessions.csv`, keep total room cost at or below `$800`, and make any later coordinator update easy to apply without discarding correct completed work.\n\nIf a newer facility update conflicts with an older room note, use the newer dated facility update for room availability.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":9,"totalLines":9,"truncated":false}},"title":"tasks/community_workshop_replan/00_room_request.md","time":{"start":1781562455950,"end":1781562455954}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_0ee9d0aab3b572b8016a307c57fd708191a5c6671edb3612cf"}},"id":"prt_ecd65b77d001DpdS3c4eu5n6E3","sessionID":"ses_1329a7efaffeLXGczGIqKMZ4Uq","messageID":"msg_ecd6599c7001xjl7E5Ggk1jOXi"}}
